    Desire: Private entities ought to be empowered to set and enforce their own normative standards, as this produces faster, more adaptive governance than public law can achieve.
    Intention: Accelerationists would actively leverage license-based enforcement and contractual terms to advance capability-friendly norms, treating private governance as a feature rather than a bug.
